<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes :  n1. The above results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at its  nmeeting held on 22 October, 2019. The statutory auditors have expressed an unqualified review opinion.  n  n2. Financial results for all the periods presented have been prepared in accordance with the recognition and  nmeasurement principles of Ind AS notified under the Companies (lndian Accounting Standards) Rules,  n2015 as amended from time to time.  n  n3. The business of the Company and its subsidiaries (the  Group ) is seasonal in nature and the performance can be impacted by weather conditions and cropping pattern.  n  n4. The Company and its subsidiaries has one reportable business segment viz-  Agri-Inputs .  n  n5. The Board of Directors of the Company had approved the Scheme of Amalgamation ('Scheme') of Zero  nWaste Agro Organics Limited (a wholly owned subridiary) with the Company pursuant to the provisions of  nSections 230 to 232 of the Companies Act, 2013 subject to necessary statutory and regulatory approvals,  nincluding the Hon'ble National Company Law Tribunal ('NCLT'). Petition for sanctioning the Scheme is  npending for final hearing before the NCLT.  n  n6. The Board of Directors of the Company had approved the Scheme of amalgamation of Metahelix Life  nSciences Limited (a wholly owned subsidiary) with the Company pursuant to the provisions of Sections  n230 to 232 of the Companies Act, 2013 subject to necessary statutory and regulatory approvals, including  nthe Hon'ble National Company Law Tribunal ('NCLT'). Separate Petitions have been filed before the  nBengaluru Bench of NCLT and Mumbai Bench of NCLT and the same is pending for hearing before the  nrespective Benches.  n  n7.Rallis Chemistry Exports Limited (a wholly owned subsidiary) had made an application to the Registrar of  nCompanies for removal of its name from the register of companies for which the approval is awaited.  n  n8. The Group has adopted Ind AS 116, effective annual reporting period beginning 1 April, 2019 and  napplied the standard to its leases, retrospectively, with the cumulative effect of initially applying the  nStandard, recognised on the date of initial application (1 April, 2019). Accordingly, the Group has not  nrestated comparative information, instead, the cumulative effect of initially applying this standard has  nbeen recognised as an adjustment to the opening balance of retained earnings as on 1 April, 2019,  nThe Group has adopted Ind AS 116 using the cumulative effect method for transitioning.  n  n9. The Group has decided to exercise the option permitted under Section 115BAA of the Income tax Act,  n1961 as introduced by the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 2019 from financial year 2020-21.  nAccordingly, there is no impact on the provision for income tax for the quarter and six months ended 30  nSeptember 2019. The Group expects to utilise the deferred tax balances partly in the current financial  nyear and partly in subsequent periods. Accordingly, the deferred tax balances have been re-measured  nusing the tax rate expected to be prevalent in the period in which the deferred tax balances are expected  nto reverse, and the resultant impact has been recognised in the current period Statement of Profit and  nLoss at the effective tax rate.  n  n10. The results of the company are available for investors at www.rallis.co.in, www.nseindia.com and www. bseindia.com.  n  n  nMumbai  n22 October, 2019  n  nFor and on behalf of  nRallis India Limited  n  nSANJIV LAL  nManaging Director &amp; CEO </in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
